@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+---
+id: task-002-track-task-createdat-and-updatedat
+type: task
+title: "Track task createdAt and updatedAt"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Record when each task was created and when it was last changed, so the app can show a task's age and
+recent activity:
+
+- Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, as ISO-8601 date-time strings; the two are equal when a
+  task is added.
+- Every change to a task (completing, reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging it) sets its
+  `updatedAt` to the time of the change.
+
+## What I did
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts`: added `createdAt` and `updatedAt` to `Task`. `r3-no-clock-or-randomness`
+  forbids `src/domain/` from reading the clock, so every function that needs the current time now
+  takes it as a parameter, `now: string`, rather than calling `Date.now()`/`new Date()` itself — the
+  same pattern the project already uses for `id` (`dl-001`).
+  - `createTask(input, id, now)` sets both `createdAt` and `updatedAt` to `now`.
+  - `completeTask`, `reopenTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag` and `removeTag` each gained a `now` parameter
+    and now return the task with `updatedAt: now`; `createdAt` is carried over unchanged via the
+    spread.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: `TaskList`'s mutating methods (`add`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`,
+  `untag`) each gained a `now: string` parameter, threaded through to the `task.ts` functions above.
+  `get`, `find`, `list`, `openCount` and `remove` are unchanged: they don't record a new point in
+  time. The `change` helper's `update` callback now closes over `now` instead of pointing directly at
+  a `task.ts` function.
+- `test/list.test.ts`: every existing call to `add`/`complete`/`reopen`/`rename`/`tag`/`untag` now
+  passes a fixed ISO timestamp (`T1` or `T2`), to stay deterministic. Added tests for: `createdAt`
+  equal to `updatedAt` on add; `updatedAt` moving while `createdAt` stays put across all five
+  update operations; and `updatedAt` staying put when `complete`/`reopen` fail (already-done /
+  still-open).
+
+Wrote the new assertions first and watched them fail (4 red) against the old implementation, then
+implemented the above (14/14 green).
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+Callers of `TaskList`'s mutating methods (the app, and any other code outside this package) must now
+pass the current time explicitly, e.g. `list.add(input, new Date().toISOString())`; this is a breaking
+change to the public API, additive only in that no method was removed.
